1.Problem Statement

Develop a menu-driven C++ graph toolkit that allows a user to create a graph, insert vertices and edges,
display the graph as an adjacency matrix and adjacency list, and execute BFS and DFS from a selected start vertex.
Display clear results for each selected operation."give a program for this"

2. Approach

1. Create a graph using an adjacency matrix to represent connections between vertices.
2. Allow the user to insert vertices and edges dynamically.
3. Display the graph using both an adjacency matrix and an adjacency list.
4. Implement Breadth-First Search (BFS) using a queue to visit vertices level by level.
5. Implement Depth-First Search (DFS) using recursion to explore vertices deeply before backtracking.
6. Display the traversal results for a user-selected starting vertex.
7. Provide a menu-driven interface that allows users to perform different graph operations until they choose to exit.

3. Conclusion

The menu-driven Graph Toolkit was successfully implemented in C++. 
It supports graph creation, insertion of vertices and edges, adjacency matrix and adjacency list representations, 
and BFS and DFS traversals. The program provides an interactive way to understand graph representation and traversal 
techniques.
